2026-11-04T15:16:14.9351263Z closures-autofix: skip-failed-recording -- THE REPAIR DID NOT HAPPEN.
2026-11-04T15:16:14.9353191Z No commit will be pushed, so waiting for one waits forever. This is
2026-11-04T15:16:14.9354264Z the case `.cursor/rules/ci-autofix.mdc` already lists as a human
2026-11-04T15:16:14.9355267Z judgment call, and its rule against re-recording an UNDER-SCOPED
2026-11-04T15:16:14.9356442Z yourself does not apply once the bot has reported that it did not.
2026-11-04T15:16:14.9357459Z A script exited non-zero WHILE being recorded, so its closure is only
2026-11-04T15:16:14.9358498Z what it reached before stopping -- and merging that would under-scope
2026-11-04T15:16:14.9359526Z the gate, which is why the merge refuses it. The under-approximation
2026-11-04T15:16:14.9360505Z this job was going to repair is real and still unrepaired.
2026-11-04T15:16:14.9361464Z Fix the failing script first; the closures job re-records on the next
2026-11-04T15:16:14.9362352Z push and this repair then happens on its own.
